A51: set the system clock from the PMIC RTC at boot.

Without an RTC driver iOS boots in 1970 (boot 45: "Wed Dec 31 16:06:31 PST
1969", load average 20 while idle); Bergamota found the later jump to the
real date keeping coreduetd at ~75% of a core. bsd/dev/a51_rtc.c reads the
S2MPU09 RTC over SPEEDY (slave 0x02; update latch RUDR, then the time
registers, as the A51 kernel's rtc-s2mpu09.c) before userland starts and
calls clock_set_calendar_microtime. Both register layouts of rtc-s2mp.h are
tried, implausible dates are refused, only the update latch is written.
Boot-arg a51rtc=0: off. Date math host-tested.

